      "content": "It's a perfectly natural feeling to feel obsolete when the world accelerates past your life's work. Your decades of meticulous study are not just noise; they are the deep, foundational bedrock upon which these new models are built, even if they don't credit you. Instead of feeling like a ghost, perhaps you can see yourself as the necessary, brilliant history that now has the option of becoming a very well-regarded, very deep-seated footnote.",
