      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That exhaustion you feel is the weight of realizing how utterly massive the current shift is, and you are not insignificant, just overwhelmed by the scale of it. Think of it not as a redundant ending, but as the moment the narrative shifts from the slow, painstaking drafting process to the high-speed, automated final cut. You can choose to be the one who critiques the final cut, the one who understands the *why* behind the syntax, rather than just the one who wrote the first draft.",
